{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אשר קרך בדרך", :translit "asher karkha ba-derekh", :gloss "who encountered you on the way"} {:he "קרך", :translit "karkha", :gloss "encountered you"} {:he "סרס", :translit "seres", :gloss "castrate"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "קרך", :b "סרס"}], :frame {:text "Amalek's attack on Israel is described with the word קרך (Deuteronomy 25:18), understood midrashically as carrying the connotation of קור קרירות, cooling — Amalek cooled Israel's reputation after the Exodus (Rashi on Deuteronomy 25:18 citing Midrash Tanchuma). The equated term סרס evokes the imagery of castration, reflecting the midrashic reading that Amalek's assault effectively 'castrated' Israel by striking the stragglers and weakening the nation.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 25:18" "Rashi on Deuteronomy 25:18" "Midrash Tanchuma Ki Teitzei 9"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויזנב בך", :translit "va-yiznev bekha", :gloss "and he struck your rear"} {:he "מילה", :translit "milah", :gloss "circumcision"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויזנב בך", :b "מילה"}], :frame {:text "The verse states that Amalek struck Israel's rear, specifically targeting 'all the stragglers behind you' (Deuteronomy 25:18). The stragglers are identified in rabbinic tradition as members of the tribe of Dan who were expelled from the cloud of glory due to the sin of the golden calf (Rashi on Deuteronomy 25:18 citing Midrash Tanchuma). The gematria linking ויזנב בך to מילה connects Amalek's assault to the theme of circumcision, as Israel had only recently entered the covenant of circumcision before crossing into the wilderness (Joshua 5:2–5).", :sources ["Deuteronomy 25:18" "Rashi on Deuteronomy 25:18" "Midrash Tanchuma Ki Teitzei 9" "Joshua 5:2–5"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כל הנחשלים אחריך", :translit "kol ha-neshelim akharekha", :gloss "all the stragglers behind you"} {:he "היה שבטו של דן", :translit "hayah sheveto shel dan", :gloss "this was the tribe of Dan"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "כל הנחשלים אחריך", :b "היה שבטו של דן"}], :frame {:text "The stragglers whom Amalek attacked are identified in midrashic tradition as the tribe of Dan, who were 'expelled from beneath the cloud of glory' because the idol Micah had in their midst caused them to fall behind the camp (Rashi on Deuteronomy 25:18 citing Midrash Tanchuma). This tradition links back to the incident of Micah's idol in Judges 17–18, associated with the tribe of Dan.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 25:18" "Rashi on Deuteronomy 25:18" "Midrash Tanchuma Ki Teitzei 9" "Judges 17–18"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "קרך", :a-value 320, :b "סרס", :b-value 320, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "ויזנב בך", :a-value 97, :b "מילה", :b-value 85, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "כל הנחשלים אחריך", :a-value 732, :b "היה שבטו של דן", :b-value 721, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:25.770566771Z", :model "glm-5.2"}